{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217288-new-merit-staff","id":1217288,"title":"New Merit: Staff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-10T00:42:15-07:00","id":1217288,"title":"New Merit: Staff","content":"I had originally wanted <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086069-my-first-exalted-character\">Hakaan</a> to have a gaggle of students following him around, but none of the core Merits really fit the concept. They're not soldiers, nor organized with military discipline (Command); and their loyalty is to the University rather than Hakaan himself (Retainers &amp; Followers). This, then, is my attempt to patch a hole in Ex3:<br /> <br /> <b>Staff</b> (\u2022\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Equivalent level of Backing<br /> The character has been assigned a number of aides, assistants, gofers, etc., by the organization Backing her. These can be clerks, scribes, accountants, researchers, graduate students, etc.<br /> <br /> A two-dot staff consists of five young men or women in entry-level positions: one- or two-dot Attributes, with two or three appropriate Abilities at one dot each.<br /> <br /> Three dots provides the character with a staff of ten people, including two or three careerists with two Abilities at the two-dot level, and two others at one dot each.<br /> <br /> Four dots' worth of Staff mean the character directs twenty individuals, including an adjutant of noteworthy skill: three dots in an appropriate Attribute, plus a three-dot Ability (Lore for a senior researcher, Linguistics for a master scribe, etc.; if no Ability seems appropriate, Bureaucracy makes a good fallback), two Abilities with two dots each, and two more at one dot each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:19:59-07:00","id":1217292,"title":"","content":"I'd just use followers and specify that those particular followers are loyal to the university, not the char. Because it seems what you want is basically the followers background and all Staff is is essentially a more expensive, less good variant of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:43:01-07:00","id":1217293,"title":"","content":"If they're loyal to the university, not the character, that's already covered by Backing. Backing already specifies that your character can have subordinates relative to your position in your organization, and the power of that organization. A professor doesn't need an additional Merit for staff the university provides. That's one of the perks of the Backing Merit already.<br /> <br /> Backing keeps things abstract because... underlings that aren't combatants or socially oriented they don't have a significant function in the system besides existing. Most underlings provided by station within a group are going to basically be there handle Leadership Project failure conditions for you (which is unrolled anyway).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T01:47:19-07:00","id":1217295,"title":"","content":"Backing already represents the <i>support and assistance</i> you can draw from having standing in an organisation, while \u200bAllies represent having a noteworthy assistant, collegue or rhe like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T13:26:51-07:00","id":1217484,"title":"","content":"Agreed, I'd say a staff is an example of a benefit you can get from having Backing, not something you'd need to buy separately. Unless you were running a very specific type of game (say, where everyone is playing faculty at the same university) where the <i>specifics</i> of your relationship to the organization is an important differentiator between characters, in which case I'd dump generic Backing all together in favor of more specific backgrounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T14:27:31-07:00","id":1217496,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure you need to dump Backing in that regard, you just need to make the interplay of Merits stronger. One character might focus on Backing and rely on their official power within the organization, while another relies on a group of Followers within the system loyal to them over the organization, while another relies more on their Influence between the different groups both inside and adjacent to the organization to get their way. And over course most characters in that environment are going to want a mix.<br /> <br /> So you can have one character that's a tenured professor as their biggest trump card (Backing), a newly employed professor who's power comes from bringing in lots of new students with them (Followers) that the university doesn't want to lose, and a dean that has sway with donors and alumni (Influence). No real changes needed besides narrowing the scope from the default the game assumes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-10T17:43:55-07:00","id":1217542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1217288-new-merit-staff?p=1217496#post1217496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure you need to dump Backing in that regard, you just need to make the interplay of Merits stronger. One character might focus on Backing and rely on their official power within the organization, while another relies on a group of Followers within the system loyal to them over the organization, while another relies more on their Influence between the different groups both inside and adjacent to the organization to get their way. And over course most characters in that environment are going to want a mix.<br /> <br /> So you can have one character that's a tenured professor as their biggest trump card (Backing), a newly employed professor who's power comes from bringing in lots of new students with them (Followers) that the university doesn't want to lose, and a dean that has sway with donors and alumni (Influence). No real changes needed besides narrowing the scope from the default the game assumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's exactly what I was thinking. By &quot;generic Backing&quot; I meant more &quot; the idea that Backing is whatever benefits you get from the organization instead of yourself&quot;. Backing, if it stays, becomes a specific type of pull within the institution. For my part I would have said the dean has Backing (official sanction from the Trustees) and the tenured professor has Influence, but that's just a matter of taste. There's still room for the OP's Staff merit to contrast the popular-with-the-students professor (Followers) with the has-a-bunch-of-research-assistants professor (Staff).<br /> <br /> EDIT: although if everyone's merits are assumed to reflect pull within the larger university ecosystem anyway, then &quot;popular with students&quot; could well be Cult, &quot;has a bunch of lab assistants&quot; could be Followers, and &quot;adviser for a bunch of PhD students&quot; could be Retainers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 05-10-2018, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}